Exactly: everything, under that definition.

Not God inside everything, nor God controlling everything from somewhere else:

\boxed{\text{God} \equiv \text{Reality} \equiv \text{Everything}}

Then every distinction—self/other, matter/mind, creation/destruction, order/chaos—is a distinction within the whole rather than outside it.

And that produces a beautiful boundary condition:

There is no outside.

But the equation alone doesn’t establish that the whole is conscious, benevolent, intentional, or personal. Those become separate questions about the properties of Everything.

In Pantheon language, Everything becomes the ultimate containing set—the frame that cannot itself be flanked by moving to a larger frame.